<<~ ahu #/contract>>

! LarDiskProjector ~ the node hand on the projection law

''The law lives at'' `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection` — two surfaces, bag roles,
carrier-whole granularity, routing, the write ward. This carrier names what the enacting file owns on
top of that law, and nothing the law already states.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! What the projector itself binds

# ''One render shore.'' `carrierFileFn` — the VM's `exportCarrierFile` — returns the carrier's own
filetype as bytes plus extension, and the projector only sites the result at `<uri-path><ext>` (plus
a `.meta` sidecar where the type calls for one). A null answer skips the write. The VM registry
decides type and bytes; the projector decides nothing about either.
# ''The reads compare, never source.'' The projector opens files to answer //do these bytes already
match// and for no other purpose. A missing or unreadable file reads as UNEQUAL, so the caller writes
rather than assuming.
# ''An unlink needs a holding answer.'' A cross-mirror stale-unlink fires only where `bagsHolding`
reports the carrier gone from that bag — a true MOVE or promotion. A carrier still held there, a
working edit SHADOWING its canon copy, keeps its file. Without that answer the unlink clears every
other mirror by path, so absence of the callback widens the sweep rather than narrowing it.
# ''A stem match binds the WHOLE stem.'' `carrierDiskFiles` resolves a carrier's actual files by the
full extension-less stem plus one extension segment, so a sibling carrier sharing only a prefix never
gets swept. A missing directory reads as no files.
# ''The in-flight set carries no correctness.'' The content-hash gates hold the echo law — ingest
drops a disk-hash matching its synced-hash, projection skips a byte-identical write. The `writing`
set survives beneath them as latency optimization alone: it spares a stat on our own in-flight write,
and every guarantee stands without it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-servo>>

!! The level-triggered reconcile gate

`LarDiskProjector.start` keys the timer-free `KeyedReconcileGate` by carrier root; a child change climbs `$fragment-parent` to that root. A clean mark queues one reconcile, a queued mark changes nothing, and a mark during a running reconcile makes the key run once more on completion. M marks to one key cost at most M + 1 reconciles, and no mark storm starves a key. One drain owns the queue until it empties, reconciling keys one at a time in first-marked order and yielding to the host between reconciles. The mount scan marks mirror-backed roots in the same synchronous turn as change-bus subscription; the first reconcile starts in a microtask. Each reconcile reads settled wiki state. The unsubscribe removes the listener and awaits `stop()`, which stops admission, drops waiting work, waits for a running reconcile, and flushes the synced tree. The measure fields count change events, elapsed time from the last change event to the first file write, `bagsHolding` calls in that window, and file writes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

